## Why This Is Asked
This tests knowledge of Azure OpenAI integration, policy-based gating, and tenant isolation in a practical chat app.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-policy retrieval from Azure Key Vault
- Input screening with Azure Text Analytics
- Policy gating before Azure OpenAI calls
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and KB in Blob
- Per-tenant auditing to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
async function handle(input, tenantId){
  const policy = await fetchPolicy(tenantId)
  if(!passesPolicy(input, policy)) return cannedReply(policy)
  const grounded = groundKB(input)
  return await openAiQuery(grounded)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test different policy rules per tenant?
- How would you handle policy updates without redeploying services?"

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical multi-tenant localization, content grounding, and integration of Azure services with OpenAI.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection and translation using Azure Text Analytics and Azure Translator
- Grounding OpenAI responses to a KB stored in Azure Blob and indexed by Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant locale settings for currency/date formatting
- Error handling and fallback
- APIM as gateway and request routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch for data flow
async function handleQuery(input, tenant){
  const lang = detectLang(input);
  const q = translate(input, 'en');
  const grounded = await queryOpenAI(q, tenant);
  const res = translate(grounded, lang, lang);
  return res;
}
```

